{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c683","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a856-93ef-7122-8c0d-478bdd3789c8"},"sequence":412,"recorded_at":1780531400000819,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78fc2956-83d9-4f46-8d12-655f5d6e9886","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78fc2956-83d9-4f46-8d12-655f5d6e9886","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78fc2956-83d9-4f46-8d12-655f5d6e9886"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a858-20b7-7603-83e8-9363b53f4c51"},"task_id":"01a0a858-20b7-7603-83e8-9363b53f4c51","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a858-20b7-7603-83e8-9363b53f4c51","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/integ-97dhxd/outcome-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-97dhxd — rework rev3 outcome (review findings F6, F7)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review` via handoff).\n4|Candidate: uncommitted in Story worktree, branch tip unchanged at `7d2126a`.\n5|F1–F5 preserved as accepted; no generator rerun (no scaffold change this round).\n6|\n7|## F6 — logout/login supersede in-flight restore/refresh/select (blocking, fixed)\n8|\n9|Root cause (confirmed by reproducing all three reviewer attacks on the\n10|candidate before the fix): `logout()` bumped `generation` but\n11|`restoreSession`/`restoreInstallations`/`refreshInstallations`/\n12|`selectInstallation`/`currentToken` never captured or re-checked it, so a\n13|continuation landing after logout/new login revived the session, re-saved\n14|the identity, and emitted state. The token-refresh helper could also save\n15|refreshed tokens after logout.\n16|\n17|Fix (production call sites):\n18|\n19|- `GitHubAuth.Flow` (`Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/GitHubAuth+Flow.swift`):\n20|  `beginLogin`/`cancelLogin`/`logout` bump `generation` and now also\n21|  `await refresher.cancelInFlight()`. `restoreSession`,\n22|  `restoreInstallations`, `refreshInstallations`, `selectInstallation`,\n23|  and `currentToken(generation:)` capture the generation at entry and\n24|  `guard !isStale(gen) else { return }` after every `await` before\n25|  mutating `session`, saving identity/tokens, or dispatching.\n26|  `CancellationError` from a cancelled refresh is a silent return, never\n27|  an error dispatch. `handlePollSuccess` gained the missing guards around\n28|  its Keychain save, identity save, and `accountVerified` dispatch, and\n29|  `loginInstallationsFailed` takes the generation and guards each dispatch.\n30|- `GitHubTokenRefresh` (`GitHubTokenRefresh.swift`): new\n31|  `cancelInFlight()` cancels and drops the coalesced task; the task\n32|  throws `CancellationError` at a pre-save `Task.isCancelled` check, and\n33|  a post-save check compare-and-deletes the just-saved record (access\n34|  token still equals the fresh value, so a newer login's tokens are never\n35|  touched) if cancel landed mid-save.\n36|- Minor, local to touched logic: `selectInstallation` now maps\n37|  revoked/unauthorized/`tokenRefreshFailed` from `currentToken` to\n38|  `.failed(relogin)`, matching `refreshInstallations` (was `syncFailed`).\n39|- Minor, local to touched logic: a 401 in `restoreSession` with an\n40|  unrefreshed expiring token (refresh failed transiently) keeps Keychain\n41|  + identity and reports `connected` + `syncFailed` for a later retry\n42|  instead of deleting a still-valid refresh token and demanding relogin.\n43|- Spec: `.spec/github-login-device-flow.md` gains a Lifecycle boundary\n44|  section and the 401-heuristic note under Session restore.\n45|\n46|Committed regression tests\n47|(`Packages/RunnerControlCore/Tests/GitHubAuthLifecycleTests.swift`):\n48|\n49|- `reviewerLogoutDuringRestoreDoesNotReviveSession` (RA1, reviewer\n50|  verbatim modulo a zero-behavior line wrap),\n51|- `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshDoesNotEmitSyncAfterLoggedOut` (RA2, verbatim),\n52|- `reviewerLoginDuringRestoreIsNotClobberedByRestore` (RA3, verbatim),\n53|- `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshLeavesNoTokensBehind` (RA4, new: logout\n54|  mid-refresh leaves Keychain + identity empty, nothing after `loggedOut`),\n55|- `refreshCancelInFlightNeverSavesRefreshedRecord` (new helper proof),\n56|- `flowRestoreWithFailedRefreshThen401KeepsTokensAndStaysStale` (new),\n57|- `flowSelectInstallationWithRevokedTokenRequiresRelogin` (new),\n58|- `userDefaultsSessionIdentityStoreRoundTrips` (new production-adapter test).\n59|\n60|Observed authentic failure first: on the pre-fix candidate RA1 produced\n61|`[restoreStarted, loggedOut, accountVerified, installationsLoaded,\n62|connected]` with re-saved identity and live session; RA2 produced\n63|`installationsLoaded, syncSucceeded` after `loggedOut`; RA3 produced\n64|`connected` after `codeReceived`. After the fix: RA1\n65|`[restoreStarted, loggedOut]`, RA2 ends at `loggedOut`, RA3\n66|`[restoreStarted, loginStarted, codeReceived, failed]` (the trailing\n67|`failed` is the poll consuming the shared slow queue's next response,\n68|allowed by the test).\n69|\n70|## F7 — truthful lint scope/count (secondary, resolved as bound)\n71|\n72|Tool: `swiftlint lint`, version 0.57.0, default config (no\n73|`.swiftlint.yml` in repo), exit code 2. First-party errors: **45**\n74|(third-party checkouts + build artifacts contribute 97 more, excluded):\n75|\n76|| File | Errors | Class |\n77||---|---|---|\n78|| `GitHubTransport.swift` | 37 (36 `identifier_name` + 1 `line_length`) | Pre-existing rev1: snake_case DTO names match GitHub JSON keys; `k`/`v`; one 209-char line |\n79|| `GitHubAuth+State+Reducer.swift` | 1 (`cyclomatic_complexity` 21) | Pre-existing rev1 |\n80|| `GitHubAuth+Flow.swift` | 3 (`restoreSession` complexity 42 + body 110 lines; `restoreInstallations` complexity 26) | NEW this round: required per-await lifecycle-guard density; splitting would obscure the audit-critical guard sequence |\n81|| `Runners+Service.swift` | 2 (`identifier_name` `d`) | Pre-existing, untouched by this task |\n82|| `RunnerControlCoreTests.swift` | 1 (`line_length`) | Pre-existing |\n83|| `RunnerContainer.swift` | 1 (`line_length`) | Earlier rev of this task |\n84|| `GitHubAuthLifecycleTests.swift` | 0 errors (warnings only) | 2 reviewer-RA long lines wrapped this round, zero behavior change |\n85|\n86|No broad style cleanup performed. Lint is reported red with this exact\n87|count, not as clean.\n88|\n89|## AC coverage — 9 of 11 rows driven via committed tests\n90|\n91|Same ratio as rev2; row 7 is upgraded from sequential-only to full\n92|interleaved coverage (reviewer downgrade lifted).\n93|\n94|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n95||---|---|---|---|\n96|| 1 | App builds | BOUND (`./Scripts/build.sh` below, not a unit test) | `tuist generate` → `xcodebuild -scheme RunnerControl` → `codesign --verify` |\n97|| 2 | Real login UI drives production services | `flowLoginSuccessDrivesProductionEffectsToConnected` (+ identity persistence; UI binding manual, no UI tests) | `ManagementWindowContainer.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Flow.apply` |\n98|| 3 | Cancellation | `flowCancellationDestroysCodeAndStopsPoll`, `flowCancelWhileConnectedRestoresConnected` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.cancelLogin)` |\n99|| 4 | slow_down | `flowSlowDownIncreasesIntervalThenSucceeds`, `slowDownAddsFiveSeconds` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` + `nextInterval` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n100|| 5 | Expired code | `flowExpiredCodeFailsWithNewCode` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n101|| 6 | Refresh concurrency | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh`, `flowRefreshInstallationsWithInvalidGrantDuringRefreshRequiresRelogin` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.currentToken(generation:)` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` / `.selectInstallation` |\n102|| 7 | Logout + interleaving | `reviewerLogoutDuringRestoreDoesNotReviveSession`, `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshDoesNotEmitSyncAfterLoggedOut`, `reviewerLoginDuringRestoreIsNotClobberedByRestore`, `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshLeavesNoTokensBehind`, `refreshCancelInFlightNeverSavesRefreshedRecord`, `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync`, restore/401/select/UserDefaults tests | `Flow.apply(.logout)` vs `.restoreSession` / `.refreshInstallations` / `.beginLogin`; `GitHubTokenRefresh.cancelInFlight` |\n103|| 8 | 401 | `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin`, `flow401DuringRefreshRequiresRelogin`, `apiClientMaps401And403`, `flowRestoreWithFailedRefreshThen401KeepsTokensAndStaysStale` | `GitHubAPIClient.*` via `Flow.apply(...)` |\n104|| 9 | 403 | `flow403DuringRefreshKeepsConnectedWithStaleError`, `apiClientMaps401And403` | `GitHubAPIClient.fetchInstallations` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` |\n105|| 10 | No PAT fallback | `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving`, `patGuardRejectsClassicAndFineGrainedPAT`, `apiClientRefusesPATWithoutNetwork`, `devicePollRejectsPATShapedToken` | `GitHubAuth.PATGuard.validate` via device poll, API client, token refresh |\n106|| 11 | Existing menu functional | BOUND (Runners suite green; menu UI wiring manual, no UI tests) | `RunnerContainer.change → Runners.Effect.setEnabled → Runners.Flow.apply` |\n107|\n108|## Validation (real exit codes)\n109|\n110|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 64/64 passed.\n111|- `./Scripts/build.sh` (tuist generate + Release xcodebuild + `codesign --verify --deep --strict`) → exit 0, BUILD SUCCEEDED.\n112|- `codesign --verify --deep --strict .temp/products/RunnerControl.app` → exit 0.\n113|- Release `Info.plist`: `GitHubAppClientID=Iv23ligBUam7vZitsE1G`, `GitHubAppSlug=relux-runner-control`, `CFBundleShortVersionString=1.2.0`; 0 plist keys matching secret/private_key/token.\n114|- `swiftlint lint` (default config) → exit 2, 45 first-party errors per F7 table above (reported red, not clean).\n115|- Not run: `RUN_LAUNCH_AGENT_INTEGRATION=1` launchd integration (touches host launchd; default suite skips it), UI tests (forbidden), release/notary (other Story).\n116|\n117|## Narrowing mutant evidence, rev3 round (all killed, exit 1)\n118|\n119|Each mutant ran in a scratch copy (`/tmp/mutant-F6a|b|c`) with a clean\n120|`.build`; the worktree was never mutated.\n121|\n122|| Mutant | Narrowing (what it admits) | Named test that fails | Result |\n123||---|---|---|---|\n124|| F6a: drop ONLY the post-`fetchUser` guard in `restoreSession` (later guards kept) | admits session set + identity re-save after logout; later guards still block `accountVerified`/`connected` dispatches | `reviewerLogoutDuringRestoreDoesNotReviveSession` | KILLED exit 1: session live (post-logout refresh emitted `failed` instead of no-op) and `identities.load() == nil` failed |\n125|| F6b: drop ONLY the post-`fetchInstallations` guard in `refreshInstallations` (pre-`syncSucceeded` guard kept) | admits exactly one emission after logout | `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshDoesNotEmitSyncAfterLoggedOut` | KILLED exit 1: `afterLogout == [\"installationsLoaded\"]`, `syncSucceeded` still suppressed |\n126|| F6c: drop ONLY the pre-save `Task.isCancelled` check in `GitHubTokenRefresh` (post-save compare-and-delete kept) | admits overwriting the old record on cancel; post-save cleanup then deletes it instead of preserving the old token | `refreshCancelInFlightNeverSavesRefreshedRecord` | KILLED exit 1: store no longer holds `ghu_old` |\n127|\n128|Rev1 mutants M1–M8/M9d and rev2 mutants R1/R2/N1/N2/N3/W1/L1 were\n129|accepted by the reviewer and touch unchanged behavior; not rerun. No new\n130|survivors in rev3.\n131|\n132|## Bounds restated\n133|\n134|- Tokens/`device_code` never in `GitHubAuth.State`, actions, logs, or\n135|  `RuntimeLogger` (type-only). Identity store holds no secrets.\n136|- The sub-microsecond true-concurrency window between the helper's\n137|  pre-save cancel check and the save call is closed best-effort by the\n138|  post-save compare-and-delete; the load-then-delete pair is not atomic,\n139|  so a save from a newer login interleaving exactly inside that pair is a\n140|  stated residual bound (real-world tokens differ per login, so the\n141|  compare protects the newer login).\n142|- `Redaction.sanitize` still has no production caller (accepted rev2\n143|  bound: no diagnostics export in this slice).\n144|- Enterprise hosts get host-scoped endpoints; per-server App\n145|  registration + Device Flow support still required (concrete error).\n146|- No `gh` import, no PAT UI, no client secret/private key anywhere.\n147|- Root's live run reached the real GitHub authorization page in Brave;\n148|  no Authorize action taken by this run; no browser or production runner\n149|  services altered.\n150|- Work left uncommitted in Story worktree; branch tip unchanged.","final_result":true}}}
